Instruction: Read the following excerpt of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by selecting the option that best characterizes the agreement.\n\nQuestion: Is the 'financial point of view' the sole consideration when determining whether an offer qualifies as superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement Excerpt: Section 8.3 Evaluation Criteria. Notwithstanding any apparently conflicting provisions, if the Board receives a third-party bid, it shall determine whether the bid qualifies as a Superior Offer by (i) evaluating the bid’s financial terms in consultation with experienced financial analysts; (ii) taking into account qualitative factors such as strategic market positioning, competitive dynamics, and regulatory risk, as advised by the company’s external legal counsel; (iii) entering a defined negotiation period with the bidding party to address any discrepancies between financial proposals and non-financial considerations; and (iv) requiring that any amendment to the financial terms triggers a comprehensive review that includes non-financial metrics. (Pages 102-103)
